  "$comment": "Shared core buildings (docs/06-economy.md §1). Order = type index in PlaceBuilding commands. size S/M/L = 2x2/3x3/4x4 tile footprint; placement land = buildable tiles, mountain = mountain tiles (mines); territory = claim radius once complete; storage = holds a goods stock once complete; carriers = carriers homed at the building once complete (refilled 1 per 60 s; the start castle starts full); cost = construction materials; production = work cycle of a complete building: optional inputs {good: amount} taken from its input piles at the start (a key \"a|b|c\" is one pile accepting any of the goods, e.g. mine food), optional harvest within radius tiles of its centre in own territory (tree/stone/game object, fish resource or coal/iron_ore/gold_ore deposit: one unit taken at the end; water/fertile terrain: only required), one output unit into its output pile after ticks (10 ticks = 1 s); a smith lists \"outputs\" instead of \"output\" and makes the one its owner's quota picks each cycle (one output pile per good); a cycle runs only while the worker is inside, who is an idle carrier that fetched the optional \"tool\" good from a storage on its way (docs/06-economy.md §3). Costs are ASSUMPTIONS to be tuned in playtests.",
